questions.prompt:
A `<ul>` holds two `<li class="i">` elements. You run the code below. What do the two `console.log` calls print?

```js
const live = document.getElementsByClassName('i');
const snap = document.querySelectorAll('.i');
const li = document.createElement('li');
li.className = 'i';
document.querySelector('ul').append(li);
console.log(live.length, snap.length);
```

